        "content": "<p>ChihweiLHBird opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/15056\">PR #15056</a> from <code>ChihweiLHBird:wasi-nn-onnx-input-types</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The ONNX backend can decode only <code>f32</code> input tensors. For other types, <code>compute</code> returns <code>UnsupportedTensorType</code>, so models that take <code>i64</code> token IDs cannot run.</p>\n<p>This change decodes input tensors of all seven wasi-nn tensor types with one generic helper. For <code>f16</code> and <code>bf16</code>, it turns on the <code>half</code> feature of <code>ort</code> and adds <code>half</code> as a dependency. <code>half</code> 2.4.1 is already in <code>Cargo.lock</code>, so no new crate comes in. The setup step now also accepts models with <code>f16</code> and <code>bf16</code> tensors. The change also removes <code>bytes_to_f32_vec</code>, which has no users now.</p>\n<p>Outputs are still <code>f32</code> only. That can be a follow-up.</p>\n<p>CI does not run the wasi-nn tests. To run the new unit tests:</p>\n<p><div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">cargo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">test</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">p</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">wasmtime</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">wasi</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">nn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">--</span><span class=\"n\">features</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">onnx</span><span class=\"o\">-</span><span class=\"n\">download</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">--</span><span class=\"n\">lib</span>\n</code></pre></div><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
        "id": 635907900,
        "sender_full_name": "Wasmtime GitHub notifications bot",
        "timestamp": 1793256160
